---
import UtilityLayout from "../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Privacy & operating limits"
  description="What UtilityPot sends to Jev, what stays in your browser, and how public-page fetching and inference are bounded."
  slug=""
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Manual processing</h2>
    <p>
      Manual conversion, normalization, scheduling and diagram rendering run in
      your browser. This application has no account database, saved input
      history, session replay or input analytics. Anonymous, opt-out-respecting
      PostHog analytics measure page views and coarse tool actions, using a
      pseudonymous browser identifier in local storage rather than analytics
      cookies. SDK opt-out is stored in the browser. Pageview URLs retain the
      public path but remove query strings and fragments; referrers are reduced
      to their origin, and campaign/ad-click identifiers are discarded,
      including persisted acquisition properties. Analytics does not record form
      values, page text, provider responses, or output. Manual processing and
      downloads remain in your browser; download events measure user intent, not
      completed transfer. Hosting providers still process ordinary request
      metadata under their own policies.
    </p>
    <h2>When you choose Ask Jev</h2>
    <p>
      After explicit consent, the context described beside that button is sent
      to our Cloudflare Worker and TypeSafe. This can include sample values,
      source text, definitions, availability or questions. Do not submit
      confidential or personal information without authority. The application
      does not persist these inputs or log provider bodies. TypeSafe processing
      and retention are governed by its terms, not a claim that inference is
      fully local.
    </p>
    <h2>Public-page reading</h2>
    <p>
      Reading a public page sends its URL to our server. Cloudflare resolves the
      public hostname and fetches HTTP/HTTPS pages through its public Internet
      network boundary; URL and DNS checks repeat on every redirect. The
      destination receives the requested URL, and Cloudflare DNS receives the
      hostname. No browser cookies, authorization or provider secrets are
      forwarded. The reader executes no scripts or embedded requests, accepts
      only UTF-8 HTML/plain text, and caps reading at 250,000 bytes, eight
      seconds and three redirects. Only 10,000 characters / 100 paragraphs are
      searched, with truncation disclosed. Blocked, authenticated,
      JavaScript-only or unsupported pages can be used by pasting text. This is
      not a paywall bypass.
    </p>
    <h2>Secrets and spending</h2>
    <p>
      TYPESAFE_API_KEY is a server-side Worker secret. The browser never
      receives it. Requests are limited to 16 KB and a bounded set of
      server-authored questions; inference has a 15-second timeout and no
      automatic retries. Client and aggregate limits are 6 and 30 requests per
      minute per Cloudflare location. These limits are eventually consistent and
      are not a strict global billing cap. Provider-side spend limits are
      required before public AI launch.
    </p>
    <h2>Output boundaries</h2>
    <p>
      Typed choices and confidence do not guarantee correctness. Review
      proposals. Entity extraction is capped and may omit mentions. Source
      excerpts are not independent fact verification. Missing credentials,
      protection or valid output produce an explicit failure, not fake model
      results.
    </p>
  </section>
</UtilityLayout>
